WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.919
Okay guys, this is a fictitious critical path method,

00:00:04.919 --> 00:00:09.000
arrow diagram, for your PE application and study journey.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:15.500
We are being asked to find the minimum time and days that it will take for you to complete the project,

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:18.000
aka find the critical path.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:27.000
So a critical path is simply the sequence of stages that are needed to determine what the minimum amount of time is,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.000
going to be required to complete the project on schedule.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:41.000
So in this case, it's actually about identifying the longest period of time identified among each of these path options.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:48.000
So all we have to do is trace each of the paths and sum up their days to find the longest,

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:53.000
because this will determine what the minimum number of days will be,

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.000
that would be required to complete the project.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:02.000
So let's get started.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.000
First, we can check out the path all the way through.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:15.000
So a to b to c to d to e to f.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.000
So from a to b is 10 days.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.000
From b to c is also 10 days.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.000
c to d, 10 days.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:28.000
d to e, 5 days.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:34.000
And e to f is 1 day.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Next, we can look at point a to point c to point d to point e to point f.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.000
So this will be 15 days.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.000
c to d is 10 days.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.000
d to e is 5 days.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:04.000
And e to f is 1 day.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Then from point a to point e to point f,

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.000
this one's very easy to look at.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:22.000
It's 40 days plus 1 day.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:27.000
And finally, we can look at a to d to e to f.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:31.000
So a to d is 25 days.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.000
d to e is 5 days.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.000
And e to f is 1 day.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:41.000
So if we sum up our different paths here,

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:45.000
we can see that the first one is 36 days.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:51.000
So, if we sum up our different paths here,

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:55.000
we can see that the first one is 36 days.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:57.000
The first one is 36 days.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:00.000
The second one is 31 days.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.000
The third one is 41 days.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:09.000
And the fourth one is 31 days.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:13.000
So our critical path, AKA the shortest amount of time

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:18.000
to complete the project will be the longest or the largest number.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:23.000
So option three here of 41 days will be our correct answer.
